## Why This Is Asked

This question tests distributed systems design expertise with vector indexes, streaming recommenders, and API gateway backpressure mechanisms. It evaluates practical load testing skills beyond simple request/response patterns.

## Key Concepts

- Tail latency measurement (P95/P99)
- Vector index refresh impact on query performance
- Cache warmup and eviction behavior
- Backpressure propagation through API gateway
- Autoscaling responsiveness and cascading failure scenarios

## Code Example

```javascript
// k6 sketch to generate high-load search traffic
import http from 'k6/http';
import { sleep } from 'k6';

export let options = {
  stages: [
    { duration: '2m', target: 50000 },
    { duration: '5m', target: 50000 },
    { duration: '2m', target: 0 }
  ]
};

export default function() {
  http.post('/api/search', {
    query: 'product search',
    filters: { category: 'electronics' }
  });
  sleep(0.01);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design practical, end-to-end performance tests for streaming workstreams, including backpressure and autoscaling in Kubernetes.

## Key Concepts
- Workload modeling: ramp/steady-state
- Tail latency targets and SLA alignment
- Backpressure mechanisms and queues
- End-to-end metrics: latency, errors, lag, throughput
- Autoscaling behavior under load

## Code Example
```javascript
import http from 'k6/http';
import { check } from 'k6';
export const options = { vus: 200, duration: '30s' };
export default function () {
  const payload = JSON.stringify({ user: __VU, action: 'ingest', t: Date.now() });
  const res = http.post('https://example.com/ingest', payload, { headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' } });
  check(res, { 'status 200': (r) => r.status === 200 });
