## Why This Is Asked
Tests tail latency and real-time communication paths, not just throughput, using concrete infrastructure components (Gateway, Bot Engine, Storage). Evaluates ability to design beginner-friendly load testing with practical tooling choices and systematic bottleneck isolation.

## Key Concepts
- WebSocket load testing
- Tail latency analysis (p95)
- End-to-end vs component isolation
- Observability granularity
- Load profile design

## Code Example

```javascript
import ws from 'k6/ws';
import { check } from 'k6';

export default function () {
  const url = 'ws://example.com/chat';
  const response = ws.connect(url, {}, function (socket) {
    socket.on('open', () => {
      socket.send(JSON.stringify({type: 'message', content: 'hello'}));
    });

    socket.on('message', (data) => {
      check(data, {
        'message received': (msg) => msg.length > 0,
      });
    });
  });
}
```

